WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:09.033
In the Encyclopedia of Triangle Centers, the Soddy Line is the central axis passing through the Incenter X one and the Gergonne Point X seven.

2
00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:16.130
Extending this line reveals a remarkable incidence: it intersects the Euler line at the de Longchamps Point X twenty.

3
00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:26.611
Three mutually tangent circles centered at vertices A, B, and C with radii s minus a, s minus b, and s minus c touch at the exact vertices of the intouch triangle.

4
00:00:26.611 --> 00:00:39.080
By Frederick Soddy's nineteen thirty-six theorem, the inner and outer Soddy circles tangent to all three vertex circles have their centers X one-seventy-five and X one-seventy-six on line X one X seven.

5
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:52.220
Because the Soddy line and Euler line are orthogonal in key configurations and intersect at X twenty, the Soddy line bridges the intouch contact geometry of X seven with the Euler axis of X two, X three, and X four.
